there'd be nothing unusual about the  number of babies who died in the  neonatal unit of the Countess of Chester  Hospital until January 2015 but over the  next 18 months staff saw a significant  increase in the number of babies dying  or suffering serious collapse the reason  prosecutors say is that a poisoner was  at work  Lucy letby was a neonatal nurse at the  hospital she was also prosecuted say the  common denominator in all of the  inexplicable collapses and deaths that  she murdered seven babies and attempted  to murder 10 others some of the victims  were brother and sister some were twins  she was brought to court to hear the  jury told that hospital officials  couldn't understand why babies who'd not  been unstable suddenly deteriorated  when police were called in they found  that someone in the neonatal unit had  poisoned two babies with insulin the  prosecution says this was no accident  that the babies were deliberately  poisoned  opening the prosecution case Nicholas  Johnson KC told the jury the collapse  and deaths of the 17 children named in  the indictment were not naturally  occurring tragedies they were the work  of the woman in the dock who was the  constant malevolent presence when things  took a turn for the worse  the jury was shown what's called a  nurse's present chart recording all of  the staff who were working in the  neonatal unit listed were the names of  the 17 babies involved in this case and  the times it's alleged they were  attacked an X next to the name of all of  the nurses who were working only one the  prosecution say was present on All  Occasions and that was Lucy letby Mr  Johnson told the jury sometimes Lucy  letby tried to kill the same baby more  than once sometimes a baby she succeeded  in killing she didn't manage to kill the  first time she tried or even the second  time and in one case even the third time  Lucy letby's parents were in court to  hear the case against her so two family  members of some of her alleged child  victims a court order prevents the  reporting of anything that could  identify the babies or their parents  the court heard Lucy letby took an  unusual interest in the families of some  of the babies who died she'd search for  them online and tracked one on Facebook  she denies all 22 counts of murder and  attempted murder and the trial continues  Greg Milam Sky News Manchester
 

